  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 138 AM MDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nOn Tuesday, the upper high continues to meander over NM but\nmay weaken another decameter. In addition to the high terrain\nstorms, it also looks like a boundary over northeast NM will\nbecome a focus for storms and heavy rainfall. That boundary will\nlikely get pushed southward with the convection Tuesday night, but\nshould loose its identity by Wednesday morning. The upper high\nwill continue to meander over NM through Thursday with daily\nrounds of shower and thunderstorm activity focused over the high\nterrain. The high will shift westward slightly on Friday and re- \nstrengthen to 599-600dam near or just southwest of the Four \nCorners. This will open the door for another weak boundary to move\ninto NE NM late Thursday into Friday which will be an additional \nfocus for storm development on Friday. This boundary or perhaps a \ndifferent one may also be in play for Saturday across eastern NM.\nAll-in-all, typical monsoon hazard are in play through the week\nincluding heavy rainfall, localized flash flooding and gusty\noutflow winds.",
